permission to control if the directory may be searched.  File ac‐
cess permissions are interpreted by the system as they  apply  to
three  different  classes  of users: the owner of the file, those
users in the file’s group, anyone else.  Every file has an  inde‐
pendent  set  of  access  permissions  for each of these classes.
